  "title": "Blockbuster Passed on Netflix for $50 Million",
  "description": "In 2000, Blockbuster could have bought Netflix for 50 million dollars.\n\nSources:\n- Wikipedia: Netflix: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Netflix\n- Wikipedia: Blockbuster LLC: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blockbuster_LLC\n\nFrom Wikipedia (Blockbuster LLC): in 2000 Blockbuster turned down a chance to buy the fledgling Netflix for $50 million; at its peak in 2004 it operated 9,094 stores; it filed for bankruptcy protection in 2010; one franchised store remains, in Bend, Oregon. From Wikipedia (Netflix): Netflix was founded by Marc Randolph and Reed Hastings as a DVD rental service on August 29, 1997; it introduced a monthly subscription in September 1999; in 2005 it shipped 1 million DVDs a day; streaming launched January 16, 2007; it has 325 million paid memberships as of 2026. Not financial advice.\n\n#shorts #netflix #blockbuster #streaming #howtheymakemoney",
